   13200/    9FF2 :                     
   13201/    9FF2 :                     	; Here's how to calculate new duration values for the below instructions.
   13202/    9FF2 :                     	; Each slide of the credits is displayed for $18E frames at 60 FPS, or $144 frames at 50 FPS.
   13203/    9FF2 :                     	; We also need to take into account how many frames the fade-in/fade-out take: which is $16 each.
   13204/    9FF2 :                     	; Also, there are 21 slides to display.
   13205/    9FF2 :                     	; That said, by doing '($18E+$16+$16)*21', we get the total number of frames it takes until
   13206/    9FF2 :                     	; the credits reach the Sonic 2 splash (which is technically not an actual slide in the credits).
   13207/    9FF2 :                     	; Dividing this by 60 will give us how many seconds it takes. The result being 154.7.
   13208/    9FF2 :                     	; Doing the same for 50 FPS, by dividing the result of '($144+$16+$16)*21' by 50, will give us 154.56.
   13209/    9FF2 :                     	; Now that we have the time it should take for the credits to end, we can adjust the calculation to account
   13210/    9FF2 :                     	; for any slides we may have added. For example, if you added a slide, bringing the total to 22,
   13211/    9FF2 :                     	; performing '((154.7*60)/22)-($16+$16)' will give you the new value to put in the 'move.w' instruction below.
   13212/    9FF2 : 303C 018E           	move.w	#$18E,d0
   13213/    9FF6 : 0838 0006 FFF8      	btst	#6,(Graphics_Flags).w
   13214/    9FFC : 6704                	beq.s	+
   13215/    9FFE : 303C 0144           	move.w	#$144,d0
