   18039/    D70C :                     	; The intent of this code is to make the camera briefly lag behind the
   18040/    D70C :                     	; player right after releasing a spin dash, however it does this by
   18041/    D70C :                     	; simply making the camera use position data from previous frames. This
   18042/    D70C :                     	; means that if the camera had been moving recently enough, then
   18043/    D70C :                     	; releasing a spin dash will cause the camera to jerk around instead of
   18044/    D70C :                     	; remain still. This can be encountered by running into a wall, and
   18045/    D70C :                     	; quickly turning around and spin dashing away. Sonic 3 would have had
   18046/    D70C :                     	; this same issue with the Fire Shield's dash abiliity, but it shoddily
   18047/    D70C :                     	; works around the issue by resetting the old position values to the
   18048/    D70C :                     	; current position (see 'Reset_Player_Position_Array').
   18049/    D70C : 3215                	move.w	Horiz_scroll_delay_val-Camera_Delay(a5),d1	; should scrolling be delayed?
   18050/    D70E : 671E                	beq.s	.scrollNotDelayed				; if not, branch
