   88605/   42660 :                     
   88606/   42660 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   88607/   42660 :                     ; PATTERN LOAD REQUEST LISTS
   88608/   42660 :                     ;
   88609/   42660 :                     ; Pattern load request lists are simple structures used to load
   88610/   42660 :                     ; Nemesis-compressed art for sprites.
   88611/   42660 :                     ;
   88612/   42660 :                     ; The decompressor predictably moves down the list, so request 0 is processed first, etc.
   88613/   42660 :                     ; This only matters if your addresses are bad and you overwrite art loaded in a previous request.
   88614/   42660 :                     ;
   88615/   42660 :                     
   88616/   42660 :                     ; NOTICE: The load queue buffer can only hold $10 (16) load requests. None of the routines
   88617/   42660 :                     ; that load PLRs into the queue do any bounds checking, so it's possible to create a buffer
   88618/   42660 :                     ; overflow and completely screw up the variables stored directly after the queue buffer.
   88619/   42660 :                     ; (in my experience this is a guaranteed crash or hang)
   88620/   42660 :                     ;
   88621/   42660 :                     ; Many levels queue more than 16 items overall,
   88622/   42660 :                     ; but they don't exceed the limit because
   88623/   42660 :                     ; their PLRs are split into multiple parts (like PlrList_Mtz1 and PlrList_Mtz2)
   88624/   42660 :                     ; and they fully process the first part before requesting the rest.
   88625/   42660 :                     ;
   88626/   42660 :                     ; If you can find some extra RAM for it (which is easy in Sonic 2),
   88627/   42660 :                     ; you can increase this limit by increasing the size of Plc_Buffer.
   88628/   42660 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   88629/   42660 :                     
   88630/   42660 :                     ;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   88631/   42660 :                     ; Table of pattern load request lists. Remember to use word-length data when adding lists
