(1) 3724/    1029 :                     	; Basically, for any tone 0-11, dynamic volume adjustments are applied to produce a pseudo-decay,
(1) 3725/    1029 :                     	; or sometimes a ramp up for "soft" sounds, or really any other volume effect you might want!
(1) 3726/    1029 :                     
(1) 3727/    1029 :                     	; Remember on PSG that the higher the value, the quieter it gets (it's attenuation, not volume);
(1) 3728/    1029 :                     	; 0 is thus loudest, and increasing values decay, until level $F (silent)
